===Pronunciation===
* {{rfv-pronunciation|lang=en}} {{IPA|/faɪə.wɔəɫ/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈfaɪ.əˌwɔːl/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"faI.@%wO:/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈfaɪ(ə)rˌwɔl/|/ˈfaɪ(ə)rˌwɑl/}}
{{rfap|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|fire|wall|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Firewall (construction)}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[fireproof]] [[barrier]] used to [[prevent]] the [[spread]] of [[fire]] between or through [[buildings]], structures, electrical [[substation]] transformers, or within an aircraft or vehicle.
# {{computer security}} The [[software]] that [[monitor]]s [[traffic]] in and out of a [[private]] [[network]] or a [[personal computer]] and [[allow]]s or [[block]]s such traffic depending on its [[perceive]]d [[threat]].

